1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,648
They charged me five hundred dollars just to whisper my darkest secret into a cold metal drain.

2
00:00:06,948 --> 00:00:15,036
The bank promised total silence. Every payment buys another month of absolute peace from my past mistakes.

3
00:00:15,336 --> 00:00:22,944
My account balance is hitting zero. If I miss today's payment, the vault releases everything to the public.

4
00:00:23,244 --> 00:00:30,204
I begged the teller for an extension. She just pointed at the heavy vault door slowly sliding shut.

5
00:00:30,504 --> 00:00:39,216
The lock clicked. But inside, there was no escape hatch, only rows of glowing glass jars lining the walls.

6
00:00:39,516 --> 00:00:47,628
Inside each jar floated a shape. Not a file, not a recording, but a tiny, breathing human heart.

7
00:00:47,928 --> 00:00:55,824
A speaker crackled to life. The bank doesn't store secrets to hide them. It harvests them to build lives.

8
00:00:56,124 --> 00:01:04,572
Every lie I paid to bury became flesh. Down here, my silence literally grew into the people I hurt.

9
00:01:04,872 --> 00:01:11,328
The glass in front of me cracked. A hand reached out from the jar, cold and demanding my name.

10
00:01:11,628 --> 00:01:18,132
Who will you forgive today, before your voice runs out completely and takes your body with it?
